.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tenspile
creates, lists, extracts, and edits files that store tensors.
One invocation does one operation.
Short flags cluster, as in
.BR "tenspile \-tvf model.safetensors" .
A directory is the safetensors weight set inside it:
one
.I *.safetensors.index.json
if that is the only index, otherwise one loose
.I *.safetensors
file.
A lone
.I .safetensors
file beside
.I config.json
is refused unless
.B \-\-force\-single\-file
is written immediately before that path.
.PP
List and info read the header.
They do not load weight bytes, except where the format needs them:
a rawtensor manifest with
.I sha256
is verified, and big-endian or compressed data is decoded.
A rewrite streams unchanged tensor bytes into a temporary file and renames it
into place.
It keeps what it does not change: safetensors and GGUF metadata, the graph,
opsets, and IR version of an ONNX model, the pickled structure and shared
storages of a PyTorch checkpoint, npz members and their compression, and a
rawtensor manifest's
.I source
and per-tensor fields.
What it re-encodes is printed on stderr.
A rawtensor edit is appended to the manifest's
.IR history .
Deleting an ONNX initializer that a node, a subgraph, a training binding, or a
quantization annotation still names is refused.
A PyTorch checkpoint holding a value tenspile cannot write back exactly, such
as a set, is refused.
.PP
Comparison is
.BR \%tensdiff (1).
Renaming tensors into GGUF names is
.BR \%tensconv (1).
Dequantizing a pack is
.BR \%tensquant (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Exactly one operation is required.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-create
Create an archive.
Refuses to overwrite an existing file unless
.B \-\-force
is set.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-list
List member names.
.B \-v
adds dtype, shape, bytes, offset, and parameters.
A dtype is listed by its safetensors name, such as F16, when it has one,
whatever the format; other dtypes, such as GGUF block types, keep their own names.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extract
Extract members.
No names means all of them.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-append
Add members.
Errors if a tensor key already exists.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Replace a tensor key, or add it if it is missing.
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Remove tensor keys and write the archive again.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
Summarize the archive from its header:
format, version, member count, data bytes, metadata, a dtype tally,
and any notes.
On a directory, a sibling
.I config.json
with
.I \%quantization_config.quant_method
or an MLX
.I quantization
object adds one note of method, bits, and group size.
The weights stay packed.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIfile\fR"
Archive path.
If omitted, the first operand is the archive.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Longer listing.
Fields are separated by tabs.
.TP
.B \-\-columns
Aligned listing for the console, with a heading row.
Implies
.BR \-v .
Bytes and parameter counts are scaled.
Shard and detail columns appear only when a member has them.
Applies to list or info.
.TP
.B \-\-fold
Merge a consecutive numeric name segment when the tensors match.
Implies
.BR \-\-columns .
.I model.layers.[3\-5]
is one copy of each leaf, not the sum, and the offset is
.IR \- .
A gap, or a second number in the name, stays on its own line.
Applies to list or info.
.B tensdiff \-\-fold
folds a diff the same way..TP
.B \-\-sort
List members sorted by name instead of in file order.
Names are compared one dot-separated segment at a time.
A segment that is all digits sorts by its number, before any other segment,
so
.I layers.2
comes before
.IR layers.10 .
Other segments sort by their bytes.
Applies to list, and to info with
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-\-columns ,
.BR \-\-fold ,
or
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-directory " \fIdir\fR"
Directory for extracted files.
The default is the current directory.
Applies to extract.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Write the new archive here instead of replacing
.BR \-f .
Does not apply to list or info.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " name"
Container to read or write.
This build's names are printed when the name is unknown.
Which formats are compiled in is
.IR \%local/supported\-formats.txt .
.I raw
is rawtensor/1, a
.I \%.rawtensor.json
manifest plus a
.IR .bin .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable listing or info on stdout.
.B \-\-columns
and
.B \-\-fold
do not apply to
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BI \-\-dtype " name"
Dtype for a headerless input file.
A safetensors name or a canonical id.
.TP
.BI \-\-shape " list"
Shape for a headerless input, for example
.I 2,2
or
.IR [2,2] .
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata " key=value"
Set a text metadata entry on create or update.
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata\-file " file"
JSON object of metadata.
GGUF values are typed.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-header\-size " size"
Safetensors header cap.
The default is 100M.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing file on create or extract, or an existing
.B \-o
file on update, append, or delete.
A rawtensor output also checks its
.I .bin
file.
.TP
.BI \-\-force\-single\-file " path"
Read this
.I .safetensors
file even when
.I config.json
is in the same directory.
It applies only to the one path after it.
With
.BR \-f ,
it may go before or after
.BR \-f :
.B \-\-force\-single\-file \-f
.I path
or
.B \-f \-\-force\-single\-file
.IR path .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan and do not write.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the short help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH MEMBERS
A bare name selects a member for list, extract, or delete.
.PP
.I key=path
adds or replaces from a file.
A bare
.I .npy
uses its file stem as the key.
.PP
.I key=archive:member
copies one member out of another container.
.PP
A bare
.I .npz
on create, append, or update imports every array in the archive.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation finished.
.TP
.B 1
An error.
The message is written to stderr and starts with
.BR "\%tenspile: " .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List the tensors in a file, with dtype, shape, size, and offset, separated by tabs:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-tvf model.safetensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Read a large model in a terminal, with repeated layers folded into one block:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-t \-\-columns \-\-fold \-f model/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show the header, metadata, and dtype tally of a GGUF file:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-i model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Print the listing as JSON for a script:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-t \-\-json \-f model.safetensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Extract every tensor as .npy files into out/, or one tensor:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-xf model.safetensors \-C out
tenspile \-xf model.safetensors \-C out embed
.EE
.RE
.PP
Extract a quantized GGUF tensor as rawtensor, block bytes unchanged:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-x \-f model.gguf \-\-format raw \-o w.rawtensor.json blk.0.attn_q.weight
.EE
.RE
.PP
Write two tensors into one new safetensors file:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-x \-f model.safetensors \-\-format safetensors \-o layer.safetensors embed norm
.EE
.RE
.PP
Create a file from an .npy array and a tensor copied out of a GGUF file:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-cf out.safetensors w=w.npy b=model.gguf:blk.0.attn_norm.weight
.EE
.RE
.PP
Append headerless bytes; --dtype and --shape describe them:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-r \-f out.safetensors \-\-dtype F32 \-\-shape 2,4 z=zeros.bin
.EE
.RE
.PP
Replace a tensor, and see the plan first with -n:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-n \-u \-f model.safetensors norm=new_norm.npy
tenspile \-u \-f model.safetensors norm=new_norm.npy
.EE
.RE
.PP
Delete a tensor:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-\-delete \-f model.safetensors optimizer.step
.EE
.RE
.PP
Rename a GGUF model into a new file, leaving the original alone:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-u \-f model.gguf \-o renamed.gguf \-\-metadata general.name=renamed
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set typed GGUF metadata from a JSON file:
.RS
.EX
tenspile \-u \-f model.gguf \-\-metadata\-file meta.json
.EE
.RE
